Title: THE LEDGER
Author: Daniel Crowe
Draft date: June 2026

FADE IN:

INT. DETECTIVE BUREAU - DAY

DETECTIVE ROSS spreads surveillance photos across the board. DETECTIVE VANCE
marks a harbor address with a red pin.

DETECTIVE VANCE
Marcus Kline met the buyer twice this week. We stay on him.

DETECTIVE ROSS
Get Elena Ruiz in for a voluntary chat. She signed the lease on the warehouse.

INT. HARBOR CAFE - DAY

ELENA stirs her tea. MARCUS sits across from her, casual, watchful.

MARCUS
Jordan thinks we are still scouting locations.

ELENA
He drives when we move. Nothing else.

Marcus slides a napkin across the table — an address, a time.

INT. WAREHOUSE OFFICE - NIGHT

Fluorescents buzz. MARCUS opens a wall safe and lifts out a BLUE LEDGER.

He copies two pages into his phone. Footsteps echo in the stairwell.

MARCUS
Not tonight.

He locks the ledger away and exits through the loading bay.

INT. POLICE INTERVIEW ROOM - DAY

ROSS sets a photo of the warehouse in front of ELENA.

DETECTIVE ROSS
You sublet that unit to Kline Logistics. Explain the power draw.

ELENA
I rent space. I do not inventory what tenants store.

She does not blink. Ross watches her hands — steady on the table.

INT. ROOFTOP PARKING - NIGHT

Wind off the river. MARCUS loads a RED BRIEFCASE into JORDAN's trunk.

JORDAN
Tell me this is the last run.

MARCUS
One more night. Then we are clear.

Jordan pulls away. Marcus watches the city line — patient, already planning ahead.

FADE OUT.

THE END
